The '''Aix Marítima high-speed rail line''' ({{Literal translation|maritime alignment|axis}}), alternatively known as the '''''Etiopiko''''', is a {{convert|884|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} inaugurated on 19 July 1977. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|360|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}, it links the cities of [[Castejón]], [[Orquívoro]], [[Syracuse]], [[Portulegnu]] and [[Alessandria]] in 3 hours. 

In Alessandria the line merges into the [[Basilia–Alessandria high-speed rail line]], and in Castejón it branches into the ''[[Direto]]'' (towards [[Porciúncula]]) and the ''[[Daramazán–Jatiel high speed rail line|Gran Sur]]'' (towards [[Axarquía]]). 

